        'steps' => [[['h1'], 'Writing and sending a letter', "At the top: subscribers (and how many joined in 30 days, with a 12-week line), the click rate, people awaiting confirmation and unsubscribes. Compose: write the subject and the preview line (shown in the inbox), then the letter, using the Greeting, Button, Bible verse, Callout, Divider and Feature blocks. The live preview on the right shows the real letter on a computer, a phone or the inbox list. Choose who receives it and when: “Schedule” lets you write whenever you are free and pick the day and hour (in Malawi time); the letter then goes out by itself, to everyone, a segment or one person. Read “Before you send” (red items must be fixed), send yourself a test, then send. Campaigns: each letter as a card with its progress, deliveries, clicks and most-clicked link. Also Subscribers, Segments, Reports, Import and the Audit log."]],
        'tips' => ["Letters are sent in small batches so the free email service is not overloaded. A letter sent now shows its progress; if you close the page it finishes by itself.", "A scheduled letter waits on Campaigns with “Goes out by itself in …”. Until then you can change the time, send it now or cancel it.", "Every letter has an unsubscribe link, as the law requires.", "Opens are not counted (that needs a hidden tracking picture, which sends letters to Junk); clicks are counted exactly.", "The public sign-up page is newsletter.php: share it on social media."],
